OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Maps/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app
targets list `Sources` + `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,
misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` — there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real,
compiled canonical feature-page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/**` — where
every sibling P7 page ships (Admin/ApiPlayground, Admin/AuditLog, Driving/DriveDetail, …)
and which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups).
The Geofences page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Maps/**`, the faithful
equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Maps`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the same
reconciliation the sibling done-page logs recorded; it is the only deviation from the
literal prompt path. The placeholder + lint gates below were therefore run against the
REAL path `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Maps` (the nominal `TeslaSync/Features/Maps` does
not exist, so a scan of it would be vacuously clean — running the real path is the honest
check).

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is `/geofences`. A dedicated `.geofences` AppRoute case is
added (default pathSegment `geofences`, `.vehicle` group, icon `location.circle.fill`);
`AppRouteParser` already resolves `/geofences` -> `.geofences` by pathSegment (no alias
needed), and `GeofencesRouteRegistration` hosts `GeofencesPage` on it, chained into
`\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift after TripPlannerRouteRegistration. So the page is
reachable via the Vehicle-group sidebar entry and any `/geofences` deep link.
(Navigation registration is an allowed file per the prompt.)

