SUMMARY
The native SwiftUI Geofences surface ships at the repo-canonical
apps/apple/Sources/Features/Maps/** (the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
Features/Maps) as 10 files / 1977 LOC, decomposed page + @Observable model + data-source
seam + sample + strings + sub-views + route registration — mirroring the sibling done
pages. It reproduces the web PageContainer chrome (title/subtitle/Add-Geofence), all eight
web GlassPanels (the summary panel + its 4 MetricCards, the loading skeleton, the per-row
card, and the modal "Use current location" panel), the three map components via the P3
MapKit wrappers (MapContainer as a native Map+MapReader with tap-to-place — the read-only
TSMapView wrapper cannot surface the tap proxy and is out-of-scope to modify;
MapTileLayer=TSMapLayerSwitcher; GeofenceDrawer=TSGeofenceDrawer), and all four data states
(loading/empty/error/success) bound to the @Observable model with full CRUD (create/edit/
delete/toggle/inline-rename/bulk-delete), search+pin-ordered list, and the
vehicle/device/draw "use current location" flow. Radius is stored SI (meters) and shown
with the localized "m" only at the display boundary. Every one of the 66 visible strings
resolves from Localizable.xcstrings under the verbatim web i18next key names. Adaptive
across macOS/iPad (regular) + iPhone (compact) via horizontalSizeClass + #if os(iOS) guards;
a11y labels/traits on the checkbox, badges, toggle, map and actions; Dynamic Type + dark/
light + increased-contrast via the P2 tokens.

